.TH WELLNET 1 "2026" "wellutils 1.4.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
wellnet \- network overview (offline)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B wellnet
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Interfaces, addresses, Wi-Fi, routes, listening ports and traffic counters
in the unified wellutils style.
.B Strictly offline:
no sockets are opened and no requests are made; only /sys, /proc and local
state are read.
.PP
The \fBConnection\fR section classifies the primary egress interface
(routing-table lookup, no packets): Wi-Fi, Ethernet, USB tethering, USB NIC,
cellular WWAN modem, VPN tunnel (with server endpoint when detectable),
Bluetooth PAN, WiMAX, IrDA, 802.15.4 (Zigbee/Thread), Token Ring/FDDI,
dial-up PPP and virtual bridges.
.SH OPTIONS
See wellutils(1) for the shared option set (\-\-lang, --color, --plain,
--box, --json, --html, --short, --no-emoji, --debug).
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 2
Bad CLI usage.
.TP
.B 3
Runtime error.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ip (8),
.BR iw (8),
.BR ss (8),
.BR wellutils (1)
